TEXT 0 168 Left 2 ;Maximum Current with voltage source at phi=90 degree (maximum voltage)\nFrequency=1/2/pi*sqrt(1/L/C)=46270Hz->45000Hz\nCurrent = Peak Current steady state  0.4*45000Hz/50Hz = 0.4*900=360A\nCurrent steady state can by easily obtained by setting parameter  texp=50m at voltage source\nThe estimation is a bit smaller because\nnot only XC=1/omega/C gets smaller\nbut also XL=omega*L gets higher\nNOTE: At high frequencies the transients are damped out earlier because of skin effect\nwhich is not considered
